{
 "The Metal Editor stores ARGB4444, RGB565 and ARGB1555 render textures in their own formats: a program reads each channel's nearest level exactly as level / (2^bits - 1). Unbound on Metal keeps those levels (GraphicsDevice::packed_writes_round) in its 8-bit store, as each level's nearest byte: exact for 4 bits, within 1/510 for 5 and 6 bits, so the 5- and 6-bit rows differ in the last digits. The Metal Editor's draws reach 4 bits from about half precision (0.7 draws 11/15; Unbound's single-precision draw keeps 10/15), and its blend of two consecutive Blits reads the unrounded first draw (0.25 + 0.04 keeps 4/15), where Unbound packs between the two passes.": [
